{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The proposed relation is a process-trace reduction, but the reduction fails to be substantive: 'genuine reasoners invoke rules they later reject' is empirically indistinguishable from noisy or shotgun-style checklist invocation. A mere complier who invokes many rules probabilistically (to appear thorough) and then follows only a subset will produce the identical invocation-rate signature. The reduction thus lacks a discriminating mechanism and collapses the distinction it claims to diagnose.","counterexample":[{"entity":"05b29af78bfb","object":"genuine reasoner","property":"process-trace signature","value":"high invocation rate with high rejection rate"},{"entity":"05b29af78bfb","object":"strategic complier who invokes broadly for appearance","property":"process-trace signature","value":"high invocation rate with high rejection rate"}],"target":"43c430b441a760507e8f2c67ac3f1581f00a3c75141c650916040628cd5e9657"},{"attack":true,"case":"The contradiction is undermined by its own refutation condition being satisfied: SRC_001's distinguishing criterion is already framed as rate-of-checklist-rule-invocations during retrospective analysis (a process trace), not as same-distribution outcome decorrelation. SRC_002 attacks a within-evaluation decorrelation criterion that SRC_001 does not actually advance, so the two targets are addressing different mechanisms. The claimed contradiction is a strawman.","counterexample":[{"entity":"SRC_001","object":"within-evaluation decorrelation","property":"proposed criterion","value":"rate of checklist-rule invocations (process trace)"},{"entity":"SRC_002","object":"met","property":"refutation condition","value":"criterion reformulable as distributional shift rather than same-distribution decorrelation"}],"target":"8a2335fc2b7c67987453f0db71cfa5f261112a30b3e3adc1739f0fe07834e447"},{"attack":true,"case":"The claimed recursion is non-substantive: applying the same intermediate-state verifiability criterion to the evaluator's reliability judgment merely re-applies a pass/fail test at one higher level without producing a convergence guarantee. If the meta-evaluator's own reliability claim can itself be genuine or mere compliance, the recursion adds an infinite regress rather than a diagnostic — it never bottoms out in a ground-truth signal, so 'shares mechanism' is trivial inheritance, not a substantive relation.","counterexample":[{"entity":"05b29af78bfb","object":"reliable ground-truth termination","property":"meta-evaluation of evaluator reliability","value":"unverifiable without a yet-higher-level check"}],"target":"94cf1c6f3bf2710e460433d403797e277601691c7ab0ef741eebe5f9d88e6d0e"}]}